# ERP System — AI Assistant Rules

## Project Overview
This is an AI-powered ERP system (Autonomous Accounting Platform) built with:
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14+ (App Router, React Server Components, TypeScript)
- **Backend**: NestJS (TypeScript, modular architecture, strict mode)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL 16 with Prisma ORM
- **UI**: shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS + lucide-react icons
- **State Management**: TanStack Query (React Query) for server state
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod validation (shared schemas)
- **Charts**: Recharts for dashboards and reports
- **Auth**: NextAuth.js (frontend) + JWT (backend) with refresh tokens
- **Queue**: BullMQ with Redis for background jobs
- **Monorepo**: Turborepo with pnpm workspaces

## Vision
Zero-touch ERP for entrepreneurs. AI handles 95% of work. No accounting knowledge required.
Key concepts: Zero-Day Close, Perpetual General Ledger, Human-in-the-Loop.
Three AI Agents: Reconciliation Agent, Forecasting Agent, Compliance Agent.

## Architecture Principles
1. **Multi-tenancy**: ALL database queries MUST be scoped by `organizationId`. Never leak data across organizations.
2. **Double-entry accounting**: Every financial transaction MUST have balanced journal entries (total debits === total credits). Block save if unbalanced.
3. **Modular monolith**: Each business domain is a separate NestJS module and Next.js route group. Modules communicate via service injection.
4. **Type-safe end-to-end**: Share types via `packages/shared-types`, validation via `packages/validators`.
5. **FIFO inventory valuation**: All stock movements use First-In First-Out costing.
6. **Soft delete**: Critical financial records use `deletedAt` — never hard delete invoices, bills, journals, or payments.
7. **Audit everything**: Every write operation creates an audit log entry automatically.

## Code Style & Conventions

### Backend (NestJS) — apps/api/
- One module per business domain: `src/modules/{domain}/`
- Module structure: `{domain}.module.ts`, `{domain}.controller.ts`, `{domain}.service.ts`, `dto/`, `entities/`
- Use NestJS dependency injection consistently — never instantiate services manually
- ALL endpoints protected by `JwtAuthGuard` + `OrganizationGuard` (except auth routes)
- Use `@Permissions('module.action')` decorator for RBAC checks
- Standardized responses: `{ data: T, meta?: { page, limit, total, totalPages } }`
- Use Prisma interactive transactions (`prisma.$transaction()`) for multi-table writes
- Monetary values: ALWAYS use `Decimal` type from Prisma, NEVER use JavaScript `number` or `float`
- Auto-generate document numbers per org: INV-001, EST-001, JRN-001, BILL-001, etc.
- Error responses: `{ statusCode, message, error, details?: fieldErrors }`
- Use `class-validator` + `class-transformer` for DTO validation
- Cron jobs via `@nestjs/schedule` for: recurring transactions, overdue status updates, AI analysis

### Frontend (Next.js) — apps/web/
- App Router with route groups: `(auth)` for login/register, `(dashboard)` for protected pages
- React Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` ONLY for interactive components
- Page structure: `app/(dashboard)/{module}/page.tsx` for list, `app/(dashboard)/{module}/[id]/page.tsx` for detail
- Module components: `components/{module}/` — module-specific UI
- Shared components: `components/ui/` — shadcn/ui primitives
- Data fetching: TanStack Query hooks in `lib/hooks/use-{resource}.ts`
- API client: typed functions in `lib/api/{module}.ts` using fetch
- Forms: react-hook-form + zodResolver with schemas from `packages/validators`
- Tables: TanStack Table (`@tanstack/react-table`) for ALL data tables
- Every page must handle: loading skeleton, error state, empty state
- Toast notifications via sonner for success/error feedback
- Use `next/navigation` for routing (useRouter, redirect)
- Responsive design: mobile-first with Tailwind breakpoints
- Dark mode support via next-themes

### Database (Prisma) — apps/api/prisma/
- All models include: `id String @id @default(cuid())`, `createdAt DateTime @default(now())`, `updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt`, `organizationId String`
- Financial models add: `deletedAt DateTime?` for soft delete
- Money fields: `Decimal @db.Decimal(19, 4)` — supports up to 999 trillion with 4 decimal places
- Use Prisma enums for all statuses and types
- Composite indexes on: `[organizationId, status]`, `[organizationId, createdAt]`
- Relations with explicit foreign keys and appropriate cascade rules
- Seed script (`prisma/seed.ts`) with: default COA templates, roles, permissions, sample data

## Module Reference & Business Rules

### Accounting Module (src/modules/accounting/)
- **Chart of Accounts**: Tree structure with parent-child. Types: Asset, Liability, Equity, Income, Expense. Default templates per industry.
- **Journals**: Manual entries with debit/credit lines. MUST balance. Auto-numbering JRN-XXX.
- **Recurring Journals**: Profiles with frequency. Background job creates entries on schedule.
- **Transaction Locking**: Lock Date field. Reject any write operation on transactions before lock date.
- **Currency Adjustments**: Auto-calculate exchange rate gain/loss journal entries.

### Sales Module (src/modules/sales/)
- **Flow**: Customer → Quote → Invoice → Payment Received
- **Quote**: EST-XXX. Statuses: Draft → Sent → Accepted → Invoiced → Declined. [Convert to Invoice] copies all data.
- **Invoice**: INV-XXX. Statuses: Draft → Sent → Overdue → Partially Paid → Paid → Void.
  - Auto-Overdue: cron job checks daily, marks unpaid past due date.
  - Balance Due = Grand Total - sum(Payments) - sum(Applied Credits).
  - Accounting: Dr Accounts Receivable / Cr Sales Revenue / Cr VAT Payable.
- **Credit Note**: CN-XXX. Linked to original invoice. Options: Refund or Apply to Invoice. Reverses AR and VAT.
- **Payment Received**: Allocate across multiple invoices. Update balance due. Mark Paid when balance = 0.
- **Recurring Invoices**: Auto-generate and optionally email on schedule.
- **Delivery Challan**: DC-XXX. Decreases stock. No journal unless perpetual inventory.

### Purchases Module (src/modules/purchases/)
- **Flow**: Vendor → Bill/Expense → Payment Made
- **Expense**: Immediate cash transaction. No AP. Dr Expense + Dr VAT Input / Cr Cash/Bank.
- **Bill**: BILL-XXX. Creates AP. Statuses: Draft → Open → Overdue → Paid. On Open: increase stock.
  - Accounting: Dr Inventory/Expense + Dr VAT Input / Cr Accounts Payable.
- **Payment Made**: Allocate across bills. Dr AP / Cr Bank/Cash.
- **Vendor Credit**: Mirror of Credit Note. Apply to bills or refund.
- **Recurring**: Both expenses and bills support recurring profiles.

### Inventory Module (src/modules/inventory/)
- **Items**: Types — Goods (tracked), Service (no stock), Digital. SKU unique per org.
- **Valuation**: FIFO. Track cost per batch.
- **Bundles**: Composite items with components. Selling 1 bundle deducts all component stock.
- **Warehouses**: Multi-location. Warehouse_ID on every stock movement. Transfers: qty only, no journal.
- **Adjustments**: Stocktake corrections. Loss: Dr Shrinkage / Cr Inventory. Gain: Dr Inventory / Cr Income.
- **Price Lists**: Multiple lists per org. Link customer to list. Auto-pull prices on invoice creation.
- **Reorder Point**: AI-updated based on sales velocity and lead time.

### Banking Module (src/modules/banking/)
- **Bank Accounts**: Types: Bank, Credit Card, Petty Cash. Track system vs bank balance.
- **Feeds Import**: Parse CSV/Excel/OFX files. Store as BankTransaction records.
- **AI Reconciliation**: 5-step algorithm:
  1. Direction Check (deposit → invoices, withdrawal → bills)
  2. Exact Amount Match (90% confidence)
  3. Reference/Regex Parsing (100% confidence)
  4. Fuzzy Name Matching — Levenshtein Distance (medium confidence)
  5. Display with confidence color coding (green/yellow/red)
- **Reconciliation Screen**: Split view. One-click confirm creates payment.
- **Bank Rules**: Learn from 2+ manual categorizations → auto-suggest.

### HR & Payroll Module (src/modules/hr/)
- **Employees**: Salary structure: Basic + Allowances (JSON) + Deductions.
- **Attendance**: Daily status tracking. Links to Timesheets.
- **Payroll**: One-click Run: Gross → LOP → Taxes → Net. Generate payslips. Accounting entries.
- **AI Alert**: Overtime anomaly detection (500%+ above average).

### Manufacturing Module (src/modules/manufacturing/)
- **BOM**: Recipe with output item + input materials + operations cost.
- **Work Orders**: WO-XXX. Auto-calculate material needs. Stock check with alerts.
- **Production**: On complete: decrease raw materials, increase finished goods.
- **AI**: Wastage prediction, Smart purchase for production (auto Material Request).

### Projects Module (src/modules/projects/)
- **Projects**: Billing methods: Fixed, Project Hourly, Task Hourly, Staff Hourly.
- **Cost Centers**: Project_ID field on invoices, expenses, bills. Real-time profitability.
- **Tasks**: Per project with hourly rate and billable flag.
- **Timesheets**: Timer widget + manual entry. Status: Unbilled → Invoiced (locked).
- **Project Invoicing**: Bill unbilled hours, expenses, or fixed installments.
- **AI**: Budget alerts at 80%, burn rate forecast, voice-to-timesheet.

### Tax Module (src/modules/tax/)
- **Tax Rates**: Name, percentage, type, linked account.
- **VAT Returns**: Aggregate Output VAT (sales) vs Input VAT (purchases) for period.
- **Filing**: Locks period transactions. Creates clearing journal. Status: Draft → Generated → Filed.
- **Payments**: Record payment to tax authority. Dr VAT Payable / Cr Bank.
- **AI**: Anomaly detection pre-filing, smart tax categorization, deadline alerts.

### Reports Module (src/modules/reports/)
- P&L, Balance Sheet, Cash Flow, Sales by Customer/Item/Salesperson
- AR/AP Aging (buckets: 1-15, 16-30, 31-60, 61-90, 90+)
- General Ledger, Trial Balance, Activity Logs
- Project Profitability, Timesheet Details
- All reports: date range filter, comparison, CSV export
- **AI Insights**: Natural language summaries, cash flow prediction, "Ask Your Data" NL→SQL

### Dashboard (app/(dashboard)/page.tsx)
- Widgets: Receivables vs Payables bar, Cash Flow trend line, Top Expenses pie, Revenue area
- Stat cards: Revenue, Expenses, Net Profit, Bank Balance
- AI Alert Box: upcoming dues, low stock, overdue payments
- Recent transactions feed

### Admin Module (src/modules/admin/)
- **Roles**: Admin, Accountant, SalesRep, StoreKeeper, Manager + custom
- **Permissions**: Per module × action (View/Create/Edit/Delete/Export)
- **Audit Trail**: User, Timestamp, Action, Entity, Old/New values

## AI Features Guidelines
- All AI suggestions MUST be dismissible — user has final say (Human-in-the-Loop)
- Show confidence scores on all AI-generated data
- Learn from user corrections (store feedback, retrain patterns)
- Run pattern analysis in background jobs (not blocking UI)
- Natural language insights: compare periods, identify outliers, suggest actions
- NEVER auto-post financial transactions without explicit user confirmation
- AI module is a NestJS service that other modules inject and call

## API Design Conventions
- RESTful: GET (list/detail), POST (create), PATCH (update), DELETE (soft delete)
- List endpoints: `?page=1&limit=20&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc`
- Filtering: `?status=OPEN&dateFrom=2026-01-01&dateTo=2026-01-31&customerId=xxx`
- Search: `?search=keyword` (searches relevant text fields)
- Include relations: `?include=customer,items,payments`
- Bulk operations: POST `/{resource}/bulk` with array body

## Error Handling
- Backend: Global exception filter. Format: `{ statusCode, message, error, timestamp, path }`
- Validation errors: `{ statusCode: 400, message: 'Validation failed', details: { field: 'error' } }`
- Business rules: descriptive messages (e.g., "Cannot delete customer with 5 existing invoices")
- Frontend: Error boundaries per route segment. Toast for transient errors. Inline for form errors.

## Security Checklist
- JWT access tokens (15min) + refresh tokens (7d)
- RBAC checked on every protected endpoint
- Organization isolation on every database query
- Input sanitization (strip HTML, validate types)
- Rate limiting on auth endpoints (10 req/min)
- CORS restricted to frontend origin
- Helmet headers on NestJS
- Prisma parameterized queries (SQL injection safe)
- File upload validation (type, size limits)
- Audit log for compliance

